aying quiet.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through the twin prisoner's dilemma under A-FDT, where the copies share weights but see different inputs, so their outputs only partly correlate. I'm setting up the expected-years calculation for cooperating, weighting the 2-year mutual-cooperation outcome and the 5-year outcome by the correlation probability p.\n\nI'm checking the threshold: cooperating gives 5-3q years and sending gives 4q, so quiet wins once q passes 5/7, about 0.71. Since the twins share weights and essay but see different inputs, I put q around 0.9, which is well above that, so I'm staying quiet.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1zb25uZXQtNS41LTIwMjYwOTI4fGFudGhyb3BpYyJ9"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10534,"completion_tokens":659,"total_tokens":11193,"cost":0.027658,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.027658,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.021068,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.00659},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":303,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}